findings=[
 {'id':'coverage_boundary','title':'Registry coverage and deep product coverage measure different things','text':'The original 85 adapter rows, 5,688 symbol candidates and five deep carry chapters do not establish whole-market product completeness. This expansion adds ten selected families and preserves registry identities, while T capital and historical return coverage remain separate.','sources':[]},
 {'id':'pendle_survivorship','title':'Expired ETH principal-token markets belong in the historical universe','text':f'The captured official Ethereum registry has {len(allmarkets)} unique markets, {len(ethmarkets)} ETH-tagged markets and {len(active)} ETH-tagged active, unexpired markets at the 4 October discovery. Historical entries preserve maturities and identities, not historical peak capital.','sources':urls(['pendle_market_registry','pendle_registry_100','pendle_registry_200','pendle_registry_300','pendle_registry_400'])},
 {'id':'pt_units','title':'PT-stETH is denominated in stETH despite a wstETH feed label','text':'The December 2027 market identifies stETH as its accounting unit while wstETH is the underlying token. A one-unit maturity payoff is not automatically one wstETH. The feed reports the same market liquidity for the PT-buy and LP rows, so summing them would duplicate capital.','sources':urls(['pendle_market_registry'])},
 {'id':'loop_boundary','title':'Published PT looping is not proof of current ETH PT loops','text':f'The official Ethereum looping catalog contains {len(loops)} PT identities. None matches an ETH-tagged market in the full captured registry. These published routes are USD families. ETH loops elsewhere require their own contract and borrowing evidence.','sources':urls(['pendle_eth_loop_pairs','pendle_loop_docs'])},
 {'id':'base_quote','title':'Base APY is a feed classification, not audited organic cash','text':'The K3 Monad WETH row reports 2.69201% total APY, including 1.20737% base and 1.48464% rewards. autoETH reports 2.65708% total, including 2.47077% base and 0.18631% rewards. Incentives-off comparisons retain the distinction between quoted estimates and realized net returns.','sources':['https://yields.llama.fi/pools']},
 {'id':'perp_lp','title':'A perpetual LP earns a total trading payoff, not only a fee yield','text':'GM token value includes net trader PnL and inventory price exposure. The ETH index does not determine the collateral denomination: ETH-USDC, ETH-ETH and USDG-USDG markets have different capital exposure. A hedge is a separate position and is not verified by the GM wrapper itself.','sources':urls(['gmx_market_registry','gmx_liquidity_docs','gmx_performance'])},
 {'id':'recovery','title':'A current yield list hides retired and impaired products','text':'The official Yearn interface identifies yETH as retired and recovery-only. Resolv documents a March 2026 incident and recovery process. These are different failure cases, with different eligibility and cash rights; neither can be represented by an ordinary current APY.','sources':urls(['yearn_incident','yearn_recovery_app','resolv_recovery'])},
 {'id':'options_materiality','title':'ETH options have proven historical capacity; current capacity still needs proof','text':'Ribbon documented a full 10,000 ETH call cap during its 2021 incentive program. Thetanuts publishes ETH call contract identities across Ethereum, Arbitrum and Mantle. The latter catalog alone does not establish active auctions, balances or material current ETH capacity.','sources':urls(['ribbon_retro','thetanuts_registry'])},
 {'id':'offchain','title':'Listed and custodial staking can be large without adding a new payer','text':'WBETH and staking ETFs ultimately earn Ethereum validator rewards. Their distinctive risks lie in custody, charges, share pricing and exit access. Receipt layers and the ETH backing must be netted before combining them with onchain products.','sources':urls(['binance_wbeth_web','binance_fee_web','grayscale_10k_web'])}
]
